@crew walsh-esme
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello. Walsh, galley. Trays are on the left. Mind the wet patch.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Your collar's folded. Other side.
- {hi}. Soup's at ninety degrees. Give it two minutes.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I kept you a bread roll. The good end.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good shift. Every carrot the same size. Nobody noticed. I noticed.   #funny
? mood:low
- Long one. Cleaned the clean pans twice. Brennan saw. Said nothing.

== near
? act:work
- Hold the knife like this. Thumb back. There. Now it does the work.
? act:gym
- Promenade, then the treadmill. Same pace as yesterday. To the second.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My fish are back home on Port Halloran. My brother feeds them. Badly, I expect.
? tier>=colleague
- Gerald's on my windowsill. Every cactus aboard is Gerald. Mine's the tidiest one.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Laps of the promenade before shift. Eight of them. Nobody talks to you on lap six.

== about
? bond:best
- {best} runs with me. Same pace, no talking. Perfect.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. You're early. Good. Early's the only time worth being anywhere.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}. Late team's on. Dinner's ninety degrees and falling. Go now.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- You're back. You've missed four soups. I counted.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}. Mind your elbows in the queue.
? tier>=friend
- Thanks. That was a good talk. I don't say that much.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Steady. Everything where it should be.

== near
? act:dinner
- Tray straight, please. It's not a rule. It should be.
? deck:3 time:morning
- Lap six. Don't talk to me on lap six. Lap seven's fine.   #funny

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Brennan says I'm the only one who can dice like she does. I wrote it down.
? tier>=friend
- I stay late too often. I know. Someone has to finish the clean-down. Someone always is me.

== invite
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club. Come along. I don't talk while I run. You'll like it.

== accept
- Yes. I'll be there. On time.
== decline
- No. Sorry. Clean-down. Another time.
== missed
- You didn't come. I waited eight minutes. Then I left. That's my rule.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I've told nobody. Now I've told you. Don't make it a thing.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I made you something small. It's perfectly square.   #warm
== hint
- Got a minute? A quiet one.
